## systemd user service: one run of the find-missing sweep. The timer
## agent-director-find-missing.timer starts it every 2 minutes. install.sh
## --schedule fills the placeholders and writes it to ~/.config/systemd/user/
## (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/systemd/user/ when that is set to an absolute path),
## then enables the timer.
##
## Lines that start with two # are notes for you: install.sh does not install
## them. The marker agent-director-schedule below is how uninstall.sh knows the
## file is its own.
##
## To install by hand, fill the two placeholders, put this file and the timer in
## ~/.config/systemd/user/ as the user the agents run as, then run
##   systemctl --user daemon-reload
##   systemctl --user enable --now agent-director-find-missing.timer
## The Environment= lines are the ones install.sh writes: its warning prints the
## filled-in crontab lines of the cron file, and the values below are the same.
##   @@AGENT_DIRECTOR@@  the absolute path of the installed agent-director,
##                       ~/.config/agent-director/bin/agent-director, written out;
##                       in double quotes when it holds a space or another
##                       character a bare word cannot (write % as %% and " or \
##                       with a backslash; leave $ as it is: the program word
##                       of ExecStart is not variable-expanded).
##   @@ENV_LINES@@       the environment a user unit does not get, one
##                       Environment="NAME=value" line each. install.sh writes,
##                       always, Environment="PATH=<the directory of tmux>:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin"
##                       (without the tmux directory and its colon when tmux is
##                       not on the PATH of the install); then, only when the
##                       agents' tmux server lives in a TMUX_TMPDIR,
##                       Environment="TMUX_TMPDIR=<that directory>"; then, only
##                       when the install's $HOME is not the home directory of
##                       the user's passwd entry (systemd sets HOME from that
##                       entry, and the binary keeps its files in
##                       $HOME/.config/agent-director),
##                       Environment="HOME=<the install's $HOME>". In a value
##                       write %% for % and \" for "; a $ stays as it is
##                       (Environment= does no variable expansion). The result
##                       is never empty.
## Run as the agents' user, in the agents' tmux environment: find-missing run as
## another user, as root or against another tmux server can wrongly mark live
## rows missing. The config directory is $HOME/.config/agent-director, so the
## sweep needs the install's HOME (see HOME above).
## A user timer runs only while the user's systemd manager does (while the user is
## logged in, or always after loginctl enable-linger <user>).
##
# agent-director-schedule: the find-missing sweep (install-agent-director skill, schedule/)
[Unit]
Description=agent-director find-missing sweep

[Service]
Type=oneshot
@@ENV_LINES@@
ExecStart=@@AGENT_DIRECTOR@@ find-missing
